# What ships in the .vsix — written as an allowlist, not a blocklist.
#
# It started as a blocklist (`src/**`, `test/**`, …) and immediately rotted:
# `test-integration/` was added a step later, matched none of those patterns,
# and shipped inside the extension. Installing the .vsix is what revealed it.
#
# So everything is excluded and the four things the extension actually needs are
# added back. A new directory is now excluded by default, and
# `scripts/check-package.mjs` enforces the same rule from the other side —
# anything packaged that is not on its allowlist fails the build.

**

!package.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE.txt
!out/**
!media/**
